# Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (which is
# gitignored) and fill in the values; Wrangler reads `.dev.vars` automatically
# and exposes each key on the Workers `env` object.
#
# Only put RUNTIME SECRETS here. Non-secret config and resource bindings live
# elsewhere — see the inventory below so you know which file to edit when a
# value isn't behaving the way you expect.

# =============================================================================
# Runtime secrets — belong in `.dev.vars`
# =============================================================================

# Bearer token required by `POST /common-grants/admin/sync`.
# Pick anything for local dev. In production, set with:
#   wrangler secret put SYNC_SECRET
# (the cd-production workflow already does this from the GitHub secret).
#
# Example admin call once `wrangler dev` is up:
#   curl -X POST 'http://localhost:8787/common-grants/admin/sync' \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $SYNC_SECRET"
#
# Add `?force=true` to bypass the contentHash short-circuit and re-transform
# every record (use after a transform-layer fix to repair rows already in D1):
#   curl -X POST 'http://localhost:8787/common-grants/admin/sync?force=true' \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $SYNC_SECRET"
SYNC_SECRET=local-dev-secret

# =============================================================================
# Other env values — DO NOT add these to `.dev.vars`. Listed for reference so
# you know where each one lives if you need to change it.
# =============================================================================
#
# Configured in `wrangler.jsonc` (`vars` block) — non-secret, checked in:
#   PA_API_BASE_URL  Upstream PA eGrants Beta API base URL.
#   ENVIRONMENT      "preview" | "production". Set per env block in wrangler.jsonc.
#
# Configured in `wrangler.jsonc` (resource bindings) — provisioned by Wrangler,
# auto-injected into `env` at runtime; no value needed here:
#   DB         D1 database binding (database_id pinned per env).
#   SNAPSHOTS  R2 bucket binding for raw upstream snapshots.
#
# GitHub Actions secrets (NOT for local dev) — configured under
# Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions in this repo. Used by
# `.github/workflows/cd-preview.yml` and `cd-production.yml`:
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN   Token with Workers + D1 + R2 edit scopes.
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID  Account that owns the Worker / D1 / R2 resources.
#   SYNC_SECRET            Same key as above; cd-production pipes it to
#                          `wrangler secret put SYNC_SECRET` on deploy.
